---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About — Serum 66 Games">
	<section class="page-hero">
		<div class="container narrow">
			<p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE LAB</p>
			<h1>Experimental by nature.</h1>
			<p>This isn't a factory pumping out clone after clone. It’s a workbench dedicated to taking time-tested mechanics and asking, "What happens if we twist this?"</p>
			<p>Operating as a small studio means every design choice is deliberate. Every sound, line of code, and visual asset gets hand-tuned until the atmosphere takes hold. The focus isn't on reinventing the wheel just for the sake of it, but on finding those precise, unexpected tweaks that turn an ordinary session into something you can't stop thinking about.</p>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container prose-grid">
			<div><p class="eyebrow">WHY WE EXIST</p><h2>We chase the interesting idea.</h2></div>
			<div>
				<p>Modern gaming is bloated with half-baked releases, copy-paste cash grabs, and projects that lose their soul somewhere along the line. Serum 66 was built as an antidote to that slop.</p>
				<p>The goal here is simple: craft complete, tightly focused games that respect your time and leave you wanting one more round. It’s about chasing the spark of a genuinely cool concept, obsessing over the details, and delivering polished, atmospheric games designed to be played together, shared with friends, and enjoyed time and time again.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
